From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amphoze <184834775+Amphoze@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:23:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] secrets: keys and signing keys from the control plane

The two key routes and the signing-keys route answered from the process's
environment, the service_role key whatever the request said, and one made-up
symmetric signing key. They now ask the control plane with the request's own
assertion, every time, and keep nothing. The service_role key is listed only
when the request asks for it and the control plane answered it, which it does
for an owner under an assertion signed for that purpose; both key routes
answer no-store. The signing-keys route lists the project's public keys as the
control plane states them.
